    "updated_at": "2019-12-03T12:11:36Z",
    "body": "Last I checked, Chrome (and WebKit) loads an error page with an opaque origin (`data:...` in WebKit, and `chrome://interstitial` (I think) in Chrome), and does fire `onload` when a page is blocked via XFO (note that Chrome has different behavior for CSP's `frame-ancestors` because that's still handled in our renderer, but it's moving out to the browser in ~80, and aims to have the same behavior as XFO).",
